{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation in worktree ../doctor-lock-health (branch doctor-lock-health from origin/main 70679d3c21).\n\nNew module src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py (386 LOC) + wiring in doctor.py (332 LOC, both under the 800 cap). Semantics shipped:\n- Four legs reported every run: tickets-write-fcntl, tickets-write-mkdir, hlc, enrich-drain.\n- State vocabulary held/free/absent/unknown. fcntl legs probed with the same zero-deadline flock(LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB) + errno discrimination write_lock_is_busy uses, opened WITHOUT O_CREAT so a diagnostic never creates a lock file.\n- mkdir leg decodes the v2 stamp via lock_owner._parse_v2_stamp (host/ns/pid/start), liveness via _describe_stamped_pid (same-host only; 'unprobeable (foreign host)' / '(other pid namespace)' elsewhere), age via _mkdir_lock_age_s.\n- Staleness is ONLY lock_owner._mkdir_lock_is_stale(lock_dir, fcntl_held=False). No second heuristic anywhere in the module; the pid-recycle qualification and the wall-clock ceiling are inherited.\n- fcntl legs get staleness 'not-applicable' (kernel releases on holder death); the O_EXCL drain lock gets 'not-assessable' (no ownership stamp — reported with its age, never guessed at).\n- Exit code: only a 'stale' leg becomes a lock_findings entry and forces exit 1. A held lock with a live holder is INFO and keeps exit 0. Lock results live in their own list so doctor --repair's loop can never reach a lock.\n- JSON envelope gains 'locks' and 'lock_findings'; schema and the pinned help text (regenerated into docs/cli-reference.md) updated.\n\nSmoke test against the live tracker found a REAL leaked .rebar/enrich-drain.lock held ~26 days on this host — filed separately and linked discovered_from.\n\nCross-link: this is the observability half of bug sunlit-cynical-ray (84af-8d4f-bc1c-41b9), which removes the long lock hold itself; linked relates_to."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786594607113283001,"uuid":"af9effca-fc08-4947-bee0-64a6ad78d5f3"}